mode: "100644"
text: "# Source provenance and boundaries\n\nThe faceless-shorts workflow is based on the user-supplied faceless-shorts package, especially\nits README, skill instructions, six styles/*/STYLE.md files, and setup, voice, word-timing, and\ncapture scripts.\n\nThe separately supplied nafay3d_style_prompts_recreated.md says its seven style prompts and\nscreenshot-cloning prompt were newly written from public descriptions and are not the email-gated\noriginals. It also says the exact source prompts were unavailable in that extraction. Do not\ndescribe those eight prompts as original, official, or verified. The separate Untitled document.txt\nhas no provenance statement in the provided file; treat it as an unverified prompt/reference dump.\n\nThose motion-graphics prompts are not the six faceless-short styles. Keep the toolkits, style names,\nmodel details, and implementation steps separate. When relying on either prompt document, label\nwhat it says and what has been independently checked.\n"
